- the six alsoRefusedBy cases: V091, V110, V174, V181, V182 and V195.

Owner decisions. PLAN.md's Q-MAS8-A to -D lines equal the README's, verbatim. The schemas hold:
- recursionDepth and trace depth 0 to 1;
- stepRetries 0 to 3 (default 1);
- revision rounds 0 to 3 (default 3);
- attempt 1 to 4;
- a closed capability {grantDigest, toolId, manifestDigest, scope, expiresAt}, with no key material.

Reviewer probes, round 9: 34 named probes plus 2 controls (WORK/probes_r9.py, controls_r9.py), each also run on round 8. Groups:
- G: the exemption against a different gate;
- H: the exemption's edges and the sibling reach;
- F: first code and fail-closed stores;
- S: schema agreement.

Random differential (WORK/diff_r9.py): 40,000 parents with depth-1 children over three shared digests, comparing _overridden only. The 12,721 parents whose children fail their own FAIL rules are skipped. Results:
- round 8 against round 9: 249 differences. 248 go from accepted to GATE_OVERRIDDEN (the sibling reach, two printed as the C801b class, and K803's class); 1 goes the other way (K820/K821 class);
- round 9 against alt8p: 0 differences;
- round 9 against the sketch alt9: 0 differences;
- no escapes.

Timing. No command ran over 60 s; the longest took 54 s (perf_r9i: two checks of 38.9 s and 12.9 s). Results:
